54 repos described — unidentified drops to zero

Every description is extracted from what the repo actually contains: the README
bold line, the what-this-does section, or the page's own meta/title. Nothing
invented. Where a candidate turned out to be boilerplate repeated across a dozen
repos, it was rejected by duplicate-detection rather than a wordlist, because
identical text describes the estate and not the tool.

Side effect worth noting: with real descriptions the seat matcher works, and the
work-itself bucket falls from 464 to 189 as items find their actual homes. The
dumping ground was a symptom of the missing text, not of the buckets.
